<figure
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Lotus_Achaemenid_architecture.JPG/250px-Lotus_Achaemenid_architecture.JPG" height="157" width="190"

  <figcaption>Reliefs of [[ lotus flowers | nymphaea ]] are frequently used on the walls and monuments at Persepolis.

Ruins of a number of colossal buildings exist on the terrace. All are
constructed of dark-grey marble. Fifteen of their pillars stand intact. Three
more pillars have been re-erected since 1970. Several of the buildings were
never finished.

Behind the compound at Persepolis, there are three sepulchers hewn out of the
rock in the hillside.

