=== The Hadish Palace

The Hadish Palace of [[ Xerxes | xerxes-i ]] is one of palaces at Persepolis.
It's located on the east of the Palace of H (Artaxerxes I). The palace
occupies the highest level of terrace and stands on the living rock. The
inscriptions of the palace attest that the building was built by order of
Xerxes. It covers an area of 2550 square meters (40*55 meters). A double
staircase on the west leads to courtyard of the Tachara chateau and another
staircase on the northeast connects to courtyard of the Council Hall.

