== Foreign visitors graffiti at Persepolis

<figure
  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Friedrich_Werner_von_der_Schulenburg_Eingang_von_Persepolis.jpg/250px-Friedrich_Werner_von_der_Schulenburg_Eingang_von_Persepolis.jpg" height="150" width="200"

  <figcaption>[[ Friedrich Werner von der Schulenburg ]] inscription on an ancient monument at the entrance of Persepolis (Iran)

Some European travelers throughout history have left graffiti on the walls of
Persepolis during their visits.

== Accounting Records

A damaged tablet from the Persepolis Fortification Archive, dating to around
500 BC, records the distribution of at least 600 //quarts// of an unidentified
commodity among five villages, providing rare evidence that
[[ Old Persian | old-persian-language ]] was also used for
[[ everyday administration | accounting-records ]].[[ ^80 ]]

